---
// /next — the Portfolio's new foundation, deployed and visible and not yet
// replacing anything. `/portfolio` goes on being the live document until the
// ticket that flips this route; keeping both up is what lets every porting ticket
// land without taking the site down.
import FrontScreen from '../sections/front-screen/FrontScreen.astro';
import ProjectsPanel from '../sections/projects-panel/ProjectsPanel.astro';
import Shell from '../shell/Shell.astro';
---

<Shell
  title="Christian Juresh"
  description="Software engineer in London."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    {/* Nothing here is the live document yet, and nothing should index it as
        though it were. */}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
  </Fragment>
  {/* Nothing carries data-turn, and that is now the right answer rather than an
      omission: with two Sections of one screen each the document's whole scroll
      IS the page turn, which is exactly what the Kernel spans when nothing is
      marked. Marking either Section instead would put `top top` and `bottom
      bottom` on the same scroll position and make the crossing a flip — see the
      Front Screen's NOTES.md, and the Check that asserts the span.

      The stub is off the page. It was here to carry data-turn while the thing
      above the Panel did not exist; the Front Screen is that thing now. Its
      folder stays, because src/sections/stub/NOTES.md is still the authority on
      the Section convention and rehoming that is not this ticket's. */}
  <FrontScreen />
  <ProjectsPanel />
</Shell>
